    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2). Here's what I changed and why it keeps structural impact low.\n\n## What the change does\n- Accepts a structured address (`addressLine1`, optional `addressLine2`, plus the existing `city`/`postcode`), while the flat `address` stays accepted.\n- An owner is valid with **either** a non-blank `addressLine1` or a flat `address`, plus `city`.\n- Normalization (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, ST\u2192STREET etc.) applies to whichever address fields are supplied.\n- The stored/returned `address` is composed: normalized `addressLine1`, with `\" \" + normalized addressLine2` appended when line 2 is present. Because downstream reads go through this composed `address`, household hash / postcode / locality automatically use the structured value with flat fallback (city and postcode are the same field in both forms).\n\n## Files touched (6) and how each stays small\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two optional properties; dropped `address` from `required` (looser = backward-compatible, and avoids depending on advice-vs-`@Valid` ordering).\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 two fields + four trivial CC-1 accessors. Necessary for persistence/round-trip; MapStruct maps them by name so **no mapper edit needed**.\n3. **`OwnerAddressNormalizationAdvice.java`** \u2014 the composition/normalization lives here, a tiny class (low WMC_other), so adding the branch is cheap. This is the single place that composes `address`, which is the lever that makes \"everything reads structured, falls back to flat\" true without touching the readers.\n4. **`OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice.java`** \u2014 one line changed to the either/or check, plus a small `isBlank` helper (refactored from the existing `addIfBlank`, keeping CC flat).\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 two columns (this profile runs `ddl-auto=none`, so schema is explicit; h2/mysql/postgres rely on `ddl-auto=update`, matching how `postcode` etc. are already handled \u2014 so they didn't need edits).\n6. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended two trailing `NULL`s to the positional owner seed inserts.\n\nI deliberately did **not** touch `OwnerMapper`, `OwnerRestControllerV1`, `OwnerIdentityKey`, or the read-side advices \u2014 MapStruct's by-name mapping and the composed `address` field kept those out of the diff.",
